    "body": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  data-cf-product picks the accent ramp and data-cf-substrate the ash ramp, both from\n  @cloudsforge/ui/tokens.css. They are on <html> and set STATICALLY here rather than by React,\n  because a page that paints before the attributes land flashes the default ember and then\n  changes colour.\n\n  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  data-cf-product=\"beacon\" IS CORRECT, AND ITS CONSEQUENCE IS THE MOST IMPORTANT DESIGN\n  CONSTRAINT IN THIS BUNDLE.\n\n  The block exists — `ui/packages/ui/src/tokens.css:607-613` names both `beacon` and `status` —\n  and it is signal green, `#7fae5c`, deliberately the chart `good` step. The registry says why\n  (`ui/packages/ui/src/surfaces.ts:392-395`): \"for a status tool the surface agreeing with its\n  healthiest verdict is correct\". It then adds the sentence this repository is built around:\n  **\"Beacon's own pages still reserve green/amber/red for probe verdicts.\"**\n\n  So this surface's own accent is the colour of its healthiest answer, while the headline answer\n  on its landing page is frequently `refuse`. Rendering the verdict in `--cf-accent` would make a\n  refusal inherit the page's green. It is therefore forbidden: the verdict panel is drawn in the\n  reserved status tokens only (`--cf-viz-good`, `--cf-viz-warn`, `--cf-viz-crit`), and it says\n  what it is through **word + glyph + tone — three channels, never colour alone**. See the header\n  of src/lib/verdict.ts and the guard in test/verdict.test.ts, which fails if `--cf-accent` is\n  ever applied to a verdict rule in styles.css.\n  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n  data-cf-substrate=\"warm\" because the ash ramp under a green accent should not be a second\n  cool hue; `tokens.css:167` records that the estate's own reading of the two ramps was made on\n  surfaces that set \"cool\" and on none that set \"warm\", so this is the one that has had less use\n  and it is chosen on the token file's own terms rather than by copying the template.\n-->\n<html lang=\"en-GB\" data-cf-product=\"beacon\" data-cf-substrate=\"warm\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n    <meta name=\"colour-scheme\" content=\"dark light\" />\n    <!--\n      The build that produced this bundle. Stamped by the Dockerfile, read by src/lib/obs.ts, and\n      the reason an error report can be pinned to the deploy that introduced it. It is an identity\n      rather than a configuration: it names the artefact, it does not tell it where it is running.\n    -->\n    <meta name=\"cf-release\" content=\"estate\" />\n    <!--\n      The three favicons from `brand/assets/beacon/`. There is NO og card and no `og:` meta block\n      here, and the absence is read off the brand plan rather than forgotten: `brand/plan.ts:43` —\n      \"No OG card and no social banner for Admin, Lantern or Beacon.\" Those surfaces exist to be\n      opened by an operator, not shared. `brand/assets/beacon/` holds no og image, and inventing a\n      meta tag pointing at a file that does not exist is how a surface ships a broken preview.\n      test/brand-chrome.test.ts asserts the absence in both directions.\n    -->\n    <link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/png\" sizes=\"32x32\" href=\"/favicon-32x32.png\" />\n    <link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/png\" sizes=\"192x192\" href=\"/favicon-192x192.png\" />\n    <link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"192x192\" href=\"/favicon-192x192.png\" />\n\n    <!-- Not indexed, and this one is not decoration either: every route here is admin-only and\n         every panel is an operational fact about a live estate. -->\n    <meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex, nofollow\" />\n\n    <title>Beacon — release gate</title>\n    <script type=\"module\" crossorigin src=\"/assets/index-DGNTDBXA.js\"></script>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" crossorigin href=\"/assets/index-Q1C4BmdQ.css\">\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  },
